IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `sgia-seat`

-- Cases for sgia-seat.l4: what the person is told, for each question they can ask.
-- Every expected answer is written here from the text of the Act (../../registers/source-bundle/IA1965.txt) and from a calendar
-- checked with the operating system (`date -j`), not copied from the output of the code under test.
--   Sundays:   2025-12-07  2025-12-28  2026-01-04  2026-02-01  2028-07-16  2030-09-01
--   Saturdays: 2026-01-03  2026-01-10  2026-01-31  2026-02-28
--   Weekdays:  2025-12-23 Tue, 12-24 Wed, 12-25 Thu, 12-26 Fri, 12-29 Mon, 12-30 Tue, 12-31 Wed,
--              2026-01-01 Thu, 01-05 Mon, 01-06 Tue, 01-12 Mon, 2026-02-02 Mon, 2024-02-29 Thu, 2025-02-28 Fri,
--              2028-07-17 Mon, 2030-01-15 Tue, 2030-09-02 Mon
-- Where the Act does not say, the answer is the sentence "The Interpretation Act does not say."
-- An answer of that kind is asserted below as the Act's answer, not as a gap in the test.

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`no public holidays` MEANS EMPTY

GIVETH A STRING
`not covered` MEANS "The Interpretation Act does not say."

§ `The words of the law (section 2)`

#ASSERT `What does a word that the Interpretation Act defines mean` "month" EQUALS "\"month\" means calendar month;"
#ASSERT `What does a word that the Interpretation Act defines mean` "year" EQUALS "\"year\" means a year reckoned according to the Gregorian calendar;"
#ASSERT `What does a word that the Interpretation Act defines mean` "fortnight" EQUALS "The Interpretation Act does not define this word."

-- s 2(5): deemed served when properly addressed, prepaid and posted, at the time the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post
#ASSERT `When is a posted document treated as served` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS "The document is treated as served on 2026-01-05."
#ASSERT `When is a posted document treated as served` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `When is a posted document treated as served` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `When is a posted document treated as served` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `When is a posted document treated as served` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `When is a posted document treated as served` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `When is a posted document treated as served` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS `not covered`

§ `Death (section 2A)`

#ASSERT `Has the person died in law` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Has the person died in law` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the person died in law` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the person died in law` FALSE FALSE)

§ `When a law starts to apply to me (sections 10 and 23)`

#ASSERT `On which day does the law start to bind me` "named in the law or in a notification" (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS "The law starts to apply from the very start of 2026-03-01."
#ASSERT `On which day does the law start to bind me` "the date of publication in the Gazette" (Date 2 1 2026) EQUALS "The law starts to apply from the very start of 2026-01-02."
#ASSERT `On which day does the law start to bind me` "neither" (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `At what time of day on that day does the law start` "named in the law or in a notification" (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE 99 EQUALS "At midnight at the start of 2026-03-01 by standard time, which is 8 hours ahead of UTC."
#ASSERT `At what time of day on that day does the law start` "named in the law or in a notification" (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE 7 EQUALS "At midnight at the start of 2026-03-01 by standard time, which is 7 hours ahead of UTC."
#ASSERT `At what time of day on that day does the law start` "neither" (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE 8 EQUALS `not covered`

#ASSERT `On what day does a regulation take effect` (Date 10 1 2026) FALSE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS "It takes effect on 2026-01-10."
#ASSERT `On what day does a regulation take effect` (Date 10 1 2026) TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) EQUALS "It takes effect on 2026-02-01."

§ `If the law I relied on is repealed or expires (sections 11 to 18)`

#ASSERT `Does the repeal of a law affect something I had already done or become entitled to or liable for` "affect a right or liability that had accrued" TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Does the repeal do that? No."
#ASSERT `Does the repeal of a law affect something I had already done or become entitled to or liable for` "revive something not in force" TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Does the repeal do that? No."
#ASSERT `Does the repeal of a law affect something I had already done or become entitled to or liable for` "affect what was done under the law" TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Does the repeal do that? No."
#ASSERT `Does the repeal of a law affect something I had already done or become entitled to or liable for` "affect a penalty already incurred" TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Does the repeal do that? No."
#ASSERT `Does the repeal of a law affect something I had already done or become entitled to or liable for` "affect an investigation, proceeding or remedy" TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Does the repeal do that? No."
#ASSERT `Does the repeal of a law affect something I had already done or become entitled to or liable for` "affect a right or liability that had accrued" TRUE TRUE EQUALS "Does the repeal do that? The Interpretation Act does not say."
#ASSERT `Does the repeal of a law affect something I had already done or become entitled to or liable for` "affect a right or liability that had accrued" FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Does the repeal do that? The Interpretation Act does not say."
#ASSERT `Does the repeal of a law affect something I had already done or become entitled to or liable for` "something else" TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Please choose one of the listed answers."

#ASSERT `May an investigation, proceeding or remedy still go on after the repeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `May an investigation, proceeding or remedy still go on after the repeal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `May an investigation, proceeding or remedy still go on after the repeal` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered`

#ASSERT `If a law that repealed an older law is itself repealed does the older law come back` TRUE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `If a law that repealed an older law is itself repealed does the older law come back` TRUE TRUE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `If a law that repealed an older law is itself repealed does the older law come back` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered`

#ASSERT `While a replacement provision is not yet in force is the repealed law still in force` TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `While a replacement provision is not yet in force is the repealed law still in force` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `While a replacement provision is not yet in force is the repealed law still in force` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered`

#ASSERT `A law I started a case under has expired may my case go on` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `A law I started a case under has expired may my case go on` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `A law I started a case under has expired may my case go on` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered`

§ `If I am charged with an offence (sections 38 to 41)`

#ASSERT `Can I be charged with an attempt to commit this offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Can I be charged with an attempt to commit this offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `Can I be charged with an attempt to commit this offence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered`

#ASSERT `Does being penalised free me from paying damages to the person I injured` TRUE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Does being penalised free me from paying damages to the person I injured` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `Does being penalised free me from paying damages to the person I injured` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered`

#ASSERT `My act is an offence under two or more laws can I be punished twice for it` 2 FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `My act is an offence under two or more laws can I be punished twice for it` 3 FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `My act is an offence under two or more laws can I be punished twice for it` 1 FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `My act is an offence under two or more laws can I be punished twice for it` 2 TRUE EQUALS `not covered`

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be penalised under this law` 1000 FALSE EQUALS "No more than 1000."
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be penalised under this law` 1000 TRUE EQUALS `not covered`

§ `Applications to Court (sections 41A to 41E)`

-- arguments: a law provides for the application, the day it is made, no process prescribed, an old process prescribed,
-- it starts the proceedings, it is made in pending proceedings, a petition of appeal, in a class the Minister excluded
#ASSERT `By what process must I make my application to Court` TRUE (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "By originating application."
#ASSERT `By what process must I make my application to Court` TRUE (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "By summons."
#ASSERT `By what process must I make my application to Court` TRUE (Date 1 4 2022) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "By originating application."
#ASSERT `By what process must I make my application to Court` TRUE (Date 31 3 2022) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `By what process must I make my application to Court` TRUE (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `By what process must I make my application to Court` TRUE (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `By what process must I make my application to Court` TRUE (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `By what process must I make my application to Court` TRUE (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `By what process must I make my application to Court` FALSE (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered`

-- the first column of s 41D(1) becomes the second; the second becomes the first in the Family proceedings of s 41D(2); s 41E table for the SICC
#ASSERT `What does an old court term in a law now mean` "Writ of summons" (Date 1 1 2026) "any other" EQUALS "It is read as: Originating claim"
#ASSERT `What does an old court term in a law now mean` "Plaintiff" (Date 1 1 2026) "any other" EQUALS "It is read as: Claimant"
#ASSERT `What does an old court term in a law now mean` "Writ of summons" (Date 31 3 2022) "any other" EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `What does an old court term in a law now mean` "Writ of summons" (Date 1 4 2022) "any other" EQUALS "It is read as: Originating claim"
#ASSERT `What does an old court term in a law now mean` "Claimant" (Date 1 1 2026) "Family Division, Family Court or Youth Court and commenced before 15 October 2024" EQUALS "It is read as: Plaintiff"
#ASSERT `What does an old court term in a law now mean` "Claimant" (Date 1 1 2026) "any other" EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `What does an old court term in a law now mean` "Writ of summons" (Date 1 1 2026) "Singapore International Commercial Court" EQUALS "It is read as: Originating application"
#ASSERT `What does an old court term in a law now mean` "Originating claim" (Date 1 1 2026) "Singapore International Commercial Court" EQUALS "It is read as: Originating application"
#ASSERT `What does an old court term in a law now mean` "Memorandum of appearance" (Date 1 1 2026) "Singapore International Commercial Court" EQUALS "It is read as: Defendant's statement"
-- a matter 41E does not list: 41D(1) still applies (fork F18)
#ASSERT `What does an old court term in a law now mean` "Plaintiff" (Date 1 1 2026) "Singapore International Commercial Court" EQUALS "It is read as: Claimant"

§ `Fees (sections 45 and 46)`

-- arguments: a fee is payable, the exact amount cannot be known until the thing is done, the fee is paid, the estimate is paid
#ASSERT `Can the office refuse to do what I asked until I pay the fee` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Can the office refuse to do what I asked until I pay the fee` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Can the office refuse to do what I asked until I pay the fee` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Can the office refuse to do what I asked until I pay the fee` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Can the office refuse to do what I asked until I pay the fee` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered`

#ASSERT `After an estimated fee how much more must I pay or how much will be refunded` 100 120 EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `After an estimated fee how much more must I pay or how much will be refunded` 100 80 EQUALS (0 MINUS 20)
#ASSERT `After an estimated fee how much more must I pay or how much will be refunded` 100 100 EQUALS 0

§ `The Gazette (section 48)`

-- the appointed date is taken as 1 June 2026 in these cases (a borrowed fact: the date section 2 of the Electronic Gazette and Legislation Act 2025 commences)
-- on or after the appointed date the website prevails over the Gazette in any other form (s 48(6))
#ASSERT `If two forms of the Gazette differ does this form control` "the prescribed website" "print" (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `If two forms of the Gazette differ does this form control` "print" "the prescribed website" (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `If two forms of the Gazette differ does this form control` "the prescribed website" "another electronic form" (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `If two forms of the Gazette differ does this form control` "another electronic form" "the prescribed website" (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS "No."
-- print against another electronic form after that date is a pair neither (6) nor (7) speaks to
#ASSERT `If two forms of the Gazette differ does this form control` "print" "another electronic form" (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `If two forms of the Gazette differ does this form control` "another electronic form" "print" (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS `not covered`
-- before the appointed date print prevails over the Gazette in any other form (s 48(7))
#ASSERT `If two forms of the Gazette differ does this form control` "print" "the prescribed website" (Date 31 5 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `If two forms of the Gazette differ does this form control` "the prescribed website" "print" (Date 31 5 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `If two forms of the Gazette differ does this form control` "print" "another prescribed form" (Date 31 5 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `If two forms of the Gazette differ does this form control` "another prescribed form" "print" (Date 31 5 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS "No."
-- a pair (7) does not speak to, and a form against itself
#ASSERT `If two forms of the Gazette differ does this form control` "the prescribed website" "another electronic form" (Date 31 5 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `If two forms of the Gazette differ does this form control` "print" "print" (Date 31 5 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS `not covered`
-- a form the person has not named properly
#ASSERT `If two forms of the Gazette differ does this form control` "newspaper" "print" (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS "Please choose one of: the prescribed website, print, another electronic form, another prescribed form."
#ASSERT `If two forms of the Gazette differ does this form control` "print" "newspaper" (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS "Please choose one of: the prescribed website, print, another electronic form, another prescribed form."

§ `Documents served on me, or by me (section 48A)`

-- arguments: a written law authorises service, who it is served on, how, a contrary intention
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` TRUE "an individual" "delivering it to the individual personally" FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` TRUE "an individual" "leaving it at the individual's usual or last known address" FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` TRUE "an individual" "sending it by prepaid post to the individual's usual or last known address" FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` TRUE "an individual" "delivering it to the secretary or like officer of the partnership" FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` TRUE "an individual" "by email" FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` TRUE "a partnership" "delivering it to the secretary or like officer of the partnership" FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` TRUE "a partnership" "leaving it at the partnership's principal or last known place of business in Singapore" FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` TRUE "a partnership" "sending it by prepaid post to the partnership's principal or last known place of business in Singapore" FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` TRUE "a body corporate" "delivering it to the secretary or like officer of the body corporate" FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` TRUE "a body corporate" "leaving it at the body corporate's registered office or a principal office in Singapore" FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` TRUE "a body corporate" "sending it by prepaid post to the body corporate's registered office or a principal office in Singapore" FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` TRUE "a body corporate" "delivering it to the individual personally" FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` FALSE "an individual" "delivering it to the individual personally" FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` TRUE "an individual" "delivering it to the individual personally" TRUE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `May a document be served on this person or body in this way` TRUE "a trust" "delivering it to the individual personally" FALSE EQUALS "Please choose: an individual, a partnership or a body corporate."

§ `My time limit (sections 50 to 53)`

-- s 50(a), (b): 30 days from 1 January 2026 end on Saturday 31 January 2026, which is not an excluded day
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 "days" TRUE `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "Your period ends on 2026-01-31."
-- the same, but 31 January is a public holiday: 1 February is a Sunday, so the period runs to Monday 2 February
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 "days" TRUE (LIST Date 31 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS "Your period ends on 2026-02-02."
-- 28 days from Sunday 7 December 2025 end on Sunday 4 January 2026, so the period includes Monday 5 January
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 7 12 2025) 28 "days" TRUE `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "Your period ends on 2026-01-05."
-- 7 days from 24 December 2025 are not "not exceeding 6 days": the last day is Wednesday 31 December and nothing is skipped
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 24 12 2025) 7 "days" TRUE (LIST Date 25 12 2025) FALSE EQUALS "Your period ends on 2025-12-31."
-- s 50(d): in 3 days from Tuesday 23 December 2025, Thursday 25 December (a public holiday) is not reckoned, so day 3 is Saturday 27 December
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 23 12 2025) 3 "days" TRUE (LIST Date 25 12 2025) FALSE EQUALS "Your period ends on 2025-12-27."
-- s 50(d): 6 days from Monday 5 January 2026 skip Sunday 11 January and end on Monday 12 January
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 5 1 2026) 6 "days" TRUE `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "Your period ends on 2026-01-12."
-- "after" an event: s 50(a) names only "from"
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 "days" FALSE `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
-- a contrary intention in the law that gives the time
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 "days" TRUE `no public holidays` TRUE EQUALS `not covered`
-- weeks, months, years: the Act gives no rule for counting them (the worked cases)
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 1 1 2026) 2 "weeks" TRUE `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 16 7 2025) 3 "years" TRUE `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 15 1 2025) 5 "years" TRUE `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 1 9 2025) 5 "years" TRUE `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 31 12 2025) 2 "months" TRUE `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 31 1 2024) 1 "months" TRUE `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 29 2 2024) 1 "years" TRUE `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 "fortnights" TRUE `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "Please choose one of: days, weeks, months, years."

-- s 50(b) on a last day the person worked out: 3 years from 16 July 2025 worked out as Sunday 16 July 2028 includes Monday 17 July
#ASSERT `My period is in weeks months or years and I have worked out its last day does section 50(b) move it` (Date 16 7 2028) "years" `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "Your period ends on 2028-07-17."
-- 5 years from 15 January 2025: Tuesday 15 January 2030 is not excluded
#ASSERT `My period is in weeks months or years and I have worked out its last day does section 50(b) move it` (Date 15 1 2030) "years" `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "Your period ends on 2030-01-15."
-- 5 years from 1 September 2025: Sunday 1 September 2030 includes Monday 2 September
#ASSERT `My period is in weeks months or years and I have worked out its last day does section 50(b) move it` (Date 1 9 2030) "years" `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "Your period ends on 2030-09-02."
-- and Tuesday 3 September if Monday 2 September is a public holiday
#ASSERT `My period is in weeks months or years and I have worked out its last day does section 50(b) move it` (Date 1 9 2030) "years" (LIST Date 2 9 2030) FALSE EQUALS "Your period ends on 2030-09-03."
-- 2 months from 31 December 2025, worked out as Saturday 28 February 2026: Saturday is not excluded
#ASSERT `My period is in weeks months or years and I have worked out its last day does section 50(b) move it` (Date 28 2 2026) "months" `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "Your period ends on 2026-02-28."
-- 1 month from 31 January 2024, worked out as Thursday 29 February 2024
#ASSERT `My period is in weeks months or years and I have worked out its last day does section 50(b) move it` (Date 29 2 2024) "months" `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "Your period ends on 2024-02-29."
-- 1 year from 29 February 2024, worked out as Friday 28 February 2025
#ASSERT `My period is in weeks months or years and I have worked out its last day does section 50(b) move it` (Date 28 2 2025) "years" `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "Your period ends on 2025-02-28."
#ASSERT `My period is in weeks months or years and I have worked out its last day does section 50(b) move it` (Date 4 1 2026) "weeks" (LIST Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS "Your period ends on 2026-01-06."
#ASSERT `My period is in weeks months or years and I have worked out its last day does section 50(b) move it` (Date 4 1 2026) "weeks" `no public holidays` TRUE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `My period is in weeks months or years and I have worked out its last day does section 50(b) move it` (Date 4 1 2026) "decades" `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "Please choose one of: days, weeks, months, years."

#ASSERT `Is the last day of my period an excluded day` (Date 4 1 2026) `no public holidays`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the last day of my period an excluded day` (Date 31 1 2026) `no public holidays`)
#ASSERT `Is the last day of my period an excluded day` (Date 31 1 2026) (LIST Date 31 1 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the last day of my period an excluded day` (Date 6 1 2026) `no public holidays`)

-- s 50(c): directed for Sunday 28 December 2025, done Monday 29 December: in due time
#ASSERT `The day I was told to act on is a Sunday or a public holiday am I in time if I act the next working day` (Date 28 12 2025) (Date 29 12 2025) `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "Yes: the Act treats it as done in due time."
#ASSERT `The day I was told to act on is a Sunday or a public holiday am I in time if I act the next working day` (Date 28 12 2025) (Date 30 12 2025) `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "Section 50(c) does not decide this."
#ASSERT `The day I was told to act on is a Sunday or a public holiday am I in time if I act the next working day` (Date 28 12 2025) (Date 30 12 2025) (LIST Date 29 12 2025) FALSE EQUALS "Yes: the Act treats it as done in due time."
#ASSERT `The day I was told to act on is a Sunday or a public holiday am I in time if I act the next working day` (Date 29 12 2025) (Date 30 12 2025) `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "Section 50(c) does not decide this."
#ASSERT `The day I was told to act on is a Sunday or a public holiday am I in time if I act the next working day` (Date 28 12 2025) (Date 29 12 2025) `no public holidays` TRUE EQUALS "Section 50(c) does not decide this."

#ASSERT `What is the last day I may act on` (Date 28 12 2025) `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "You may act up to and including 2025-12-29."
#ASSERT `What is the last day I may act on` (Date 31 12 2025) `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "You may act up to and including 2025-12-31."
#ASSERT `What is the last day I may act on` (Date 3 1 2026) `no public holidays` FALSE EQUALS "You may act up to and including 2026-01-03."
#ASSERT `What is the last day I may act on` (Date 28 12 2025) `no public holidays` TRUE EQUALS `not covered`

-- s 50(d)
#ASSERT `Do Sundays and public holidays count in my period` 3 EQUALS "No: in a time not exceeding 6 days, Sundays and public holidays are not counted."
#ASSERT `Do Sundays and public holidays count in my period` 6 EQUALS "No: in a time not exceeding 6 days, Sundays and public holidays are not counted."
#ASSERT `Do Sundays and public holidays count in my period` 7 EQUALS "The Interpretation Act does not leave them out of a period of this length when counting its days, though s 50(b) moves a last day that falls on one."

-- s 51
#ASSERT `What clock does the law use` FALSE 99 EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `What clock does the law use` TRUE 7 EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `Is a time of day in the law standard time` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a time of day in the law standard time` TRUE)

-- s 52, s 53
#ASSERT `How soon must I do a thing for which the law sets no time` FALSE EQUALS "With all convenient speed, and as often as the occasion arises."
#ASSERT `How soon must I do a thing for which the law sets no time` TRUE EQUALS "Section 52 does not apply: the law sets a time."
#ASSERT `My time has run out may the court or authority still extend it if I apply late` TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Yes: the power may be exercised although the application is made after the time has run out."
#ASSERT `My time has run out may the court or authority still extend it if I apply late` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered`
#ASSERT `My time has run out may the court or authority still extend it if I apply late` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered`
